{"ld": 161, "paper": "HP94", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Directing the Maine Office of Community Affairs to Convene a Working Group Tasked with a Comprehensive Overhaul and Modernization of Maine's Subdivision Laws (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-ducharme-john", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bennett-richard", "s-black-russell", "s-bradstreet-richard", "h-collamore-amanda", "h-cray-dean", "h-gere-traci", "h-roberts-lovell-tiffany", "h-sayre-daniel"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This resolve requires the Department of Agriculture, Conservation and Forestry to convene a stakeholder group to review and make recommendations concerning a comprehensive overhaul and modernization of the subdivision laws in the Maine Revised Statutes, Title 12, chapter 206-A; Title 30-A, chapter 187, subchapter 4; and Title 38, chapter 3, subchapter 1, article 6. The resolve lists the minimum membership requirements for the stakeholder group. The department is required to submit a report to the joint standing committees of the Legislature having jurisdiction over subdivision review matters under those laws by December 3, 2025 and those committees may report out legislation related to that report to the Second Regular Session of the 132nd Legislature.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0094&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2026-03-09", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2026-03-09"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 161)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0094&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-787)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0094&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (H-7